
⦿ Strategy design pattern is a behavioral design pattern that enables selecting an
   algorithm at run-time.
⦿ Instead of implementing a single algorithm directly, code receives run-time instructions
   as to which in a family of algorithms to use.
⦿ In short, Strategy design pattern defines a family of algorithms, encapsulates each one and makes them
   interchangeable at runtime.

Where it is used ?
==================
➼ When multiple algorithms can be used for same task.
➼ When you need to switch logic dynamically based on conditions.

Concept explanation:
===================
• Think of an e-commerce site where discounts where discounts vary - "Festival discount", "new-user discount"
  or "no discount".
• You can dynamically choose which discount strategy to apply.

Advantages:
===========
➼ Makes the code flexible and easier to understand.
➼ Avoids complex if-else conditions.
➼ You can easily add new strategies without modifying existing ones.

Strategy design pattern
========================
⦿ Strategy design pattern is commonly asked with:
   "How will you design a flexible discount or sorting mechanism ?"

⦿ It shows understanding of Open/Closed principle (open for extension, closed for modifications).
